{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511155-literally-immortal-vampires","id":1511155,"title":"Literally immortal vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-09T14:11:27-07:00","id":1511155,"title":"Literally immortal vampires","content":"The idea popped into my head after reading some discussions about vampires and suicide and how much the beast would fight them to keep them &quot;alive.&quot; Caine's curse/blessing, as far as I remember, was that for all others would revile him, nobody could kill him in his exile. I already make my vamps borderline unkillable as is, but what if the curse of vampirism was that you literally could not die or escape your new existence, ever (except <i>maybe</i> by being diablerised - assuming your soul isn't now an unwilling roommate in another's corpse). Rather than the Final Death, filling the track with aggravated damage simply puts you into torpor and gives you an absolute hell to wake up to (seeing as the damage won't go away easily and your corpse will still be torn/burned to shreds.)<br /> <br /> How would it impact society? Rather than execution, you'd have to go to methods like tearing the bodies of criminals/enemies to pieces and scattering the body parts across the world and hope nobody ever reassembles them (huh, Egyptian mythology links?). Possibly there would be mass graves of torpored vampires, hidden from mortal sight. Population control suddenly becomes very important when nobody dies - climbing the ranks gets even uglier because not only is your boss not dying of natural causes, you can't even off him through <i>un</i>natural causes and whatever awful things you do to get him out of the way you are never free of the paranoia that he might come back for his stuff one night. Perhaps diablerie is even more common as a result.<br /> Is being a vampire a living hell for you? Well tough shit, there's no way out. Suicidal vampires would be forced to neutralise their existences by entering torpor instead. Hunting vampires suddenly becomes a multi-generational effort because the monsters simply never truly go away...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T15:03:48-07:00","id":1511160,"title":"","content":"I imagine that vampires would be much more selective and the elders wouldn't leave so much plore, because it's much more complicated to deal with an immortal neophyte than one that you can rip off the head, because if he was transformed he must be at least tough, like I said, selective, so I think without more changes the difference is that there would be far fewer immortal vampires in the world, like a hundred on the entire planet, being optimistic. If there were any that behaved more like a monster and made their existence public, it would be the same with the canon scenario except harder to suppress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T15:07:39-07:00","id":1511161,"title":"","content":"this is basically high vampires in the witcher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:25:40-07:00","id":1511167,"title":"","content":"I've flirted with the idea in the my writing. Basically, I came up with a story where vampires don't die even if burnt to ashes and the ashes are scattered. However, they are completely helpless to ever recover if damaged so utterly. A horrific fate of being blind, deaf, immobile, intelligent dust. In my story idea, vampires were fighting over a special dagger that was the only way to sever the connection between soul and dust. They were fighting over it not just as weapon, but also as the only method to euthanize loved ones by slashing some patch of dust, and as the only way to commit suicide in the far future when the entire universe was dead and there was nothing to eat or do for entertainment. Even the most immortality-loving of vampires had no desire to still be alive a googolplex of eons after entropy has destroyed the universe.<br /> <br /> Never really got around to fleshing the story out beyond that, but that was the core idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:58:46-07:00","id":1511170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511155-literally-immortal-vampires?p=1511167#post1511167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've flirted with the idea in the my writing. Basically, I came up with a story where vampires don't die even if burnt to ashes and the ashes are scattered. However, they are completely helpless to ever recover if damaged so utterly. A horrific fate of being blind, deaf, immobile, intelligent dust. In my story idea, vampires were fighting over a special dagger that was the only way to sever the connection between soul and dust. They were fighting over it not just as weapon, but also as the only method to euthanize loved ones by slashing some patch of dust, and as the only way to commit suicide in the far future when the entire universe was dead and there was nothing to eat or do for entertainment. Even the most immortality-loving of vampires had no desire to still be alive a googolplex of eons after entropy has destroyed the universe.<br /> <br /> Never really got around to fleshing the story out beyond that, but that was the core idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's even an interesting concept, but it sounds much more like a personal drama or a romance than a horror story or intrigue as the mask demands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}